# WAV masters. Never committed, never shipped.
#
# These are the Suno downloads exactly as they arrived, and ASSET_LICENCES.md
# explains why that matters: under the Terms effective 2026-09-03 the commercial
# right attaches to a permitted DOWNLOAD taken on a paid plan, so these files are
# the licensed artefacts. A later re-download on a lapsed account would carry the
# free-tier licence instead. BACK THEM UP OFF THIS MACHINE - nothing else holds a
# copy, by design.
#
# They sit at the repository root, beside licence-evidence/, rather than inside
# the app. Two reasons: they are evidence rather than app source, and anything
# under the app risks being swept into a build or an upload of the app folder.
# The shipped 112 kbps MP3s in web-sdk/apps/Ride-The-Bus/static/music/ are what
# players get; these never leave this directory.
#
# WHY NOT COMMIT THEM, given they are now licensed:
#
#   1. This repository is PUBLIC, and Suno "makes no representation or warranty
#      that any copyright will vest in any Output". If no copyright vests there
#      is nothing to enforce, so publishing a lossless master hands over a fully
#      usable asset that cannot be protected. The shipped MP3 is public anyway -
#      it is served to every player. The master does not have to be.
#   2. Five of these are 87.8 MiB. GitHub warns over 50 MiB and REJECTS over
#      100 MiB, so this is one longer track away from a blocked push.
#   3. 595 MB of incompressible audio in history is permanent. Removing it later
#      takes a history rewrite, not a delete commit, and every fork keeps a copy.
*
!.gitignore
